  "_rules": "Regression floors per subset, set from that subset's own run. Accuracy and failed calls: the looser of the run's 95% bound and the design target (a minimum takes the lower of the two, a maximum the higher); without a target, the bound with a 0.02 margin, at most 0.98 for a minimum and at least 0.02 for a maximum. Tokens, cost, latency and rate-limit waits: the upper bound times 1.5, capped at the design target unless the run already exceeds it. Cost as billed: 0. Each is rounded away from the run to its unit's step (one call for failed calls). The ci subset reports its extraction latency p95 and end-to-end latency p95 against their floors but does not gate on them: with n = 20 a p95 is the slowest one or two cases, which one slow provider call moves past any floor (docs/memory.md, 2026-10-28); the full run gates both. Floors only tighten; loosening one needs a written reason in docs/memory.md naming the run that justified it.",
